# This file ships as manifests/secrets.local.env in the deploy bundle -
# just fill in the values below directly, no copy/rename step needed, then
# run:
#
#   ./scripts/deploy-fresh-environment.sh
#
# (deploy-fresh-environment.sh reads this file directly as part of its own
# run now - no separate apply step, no cluster login/oc commands needed
# beyond the one `oc login` deploy-fresh-environment.sh already requires.)
#
# Note for repo development (not the shipped bundle): this tracked source
# file is named secrets.local.env.example so real values filled in while
# testing locally never get committed - manifests/secrets.local.env is
# gitignored. scripts/build-deploy-bundle.ps1 renames it to
# secrets.local.env (no .example) when staging the bundle, so end users
# never see or need the .example suffix at all.
#
# Only LITEMAAS_BASE_URL / LITEMAAS_API_KEY / MODEL_NAME below are REQUIRED
# before deploying - every other source (Confluence, Red Hat KCS, Slack,
# NotebookLM) already has a safe placeholder that lets its pod come up
# Ready, and gets its real value set afterward through the Streamlit UI's
# Configure popover instead (paste-a-token for Confluence/KCS, file-upload
# for Slack/NotebookLM - see scripts/refresh-slack-creds.ps1 -Mode Export /
# scripts/refresh-nbk-creds.ps1 -SkipLogin -Mode Export to generate the file
# to upload for those two).
#
# =====================================================================
# CONFLUENCE_URL (namespace: debug-agent-mcp) - OPTIONAL
#    Leave this blank to use the deploy script's built-in default (Red
#    Hat's internal Confluence instance - see CFL_HARDCODED_URL in
#    scripts/deploy-fresh-environment.sh). Only fill this in if your
#    Confluence instance is different. Email + API token are NOT set here
#    - paste those afterward via the Streamlit UI's Configure popover,
#    same as always.
# =====================================================================
CONFLUENCE_URL=

# =====================================================================
# debug-agent-litemaas (namespace: debug-agent-hub) - REQUIRED
#    The orchestrator crashes at startup (CreateContainerConfigError) if
#    any of LITEMAAS_BASE_URL / LITEMAAS_API_KEY / MODEL_NAME are missing -
#    unlike every other source, there is no safe placeholder for this one,
#    so it's the one thing that must be real before the app can come up at
#    all. Points at ANY OpenAI-API-compatible endpoint (LiteLLM/LiteMaaS
#    gateway, OpenAI itself, Azure OpenAI compat endpoint, local vLLM/Ollama).
#    IMPORTANT: no trailing /v1 on the base URL - the code appends it.
# =====================================================================
LITEMAAS_BASE_URL=
LITEMAAS_API_KEY=
MODEL_NAME=

# Second, direct-REST-call credential set the orchestrator uses independently
# of mcp-confluence-server. Optional - leave blank if you don't need the
# orchestrator's direct Confluence REST calls (OAuth login still works
# without these; this is a separate static-token path).
LITEMAAS_ATLASSIAN_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
LITEMAAS_ATLASSIAN_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
LITEMAAS_CONFLUENCE_EMAIL=
LITEMAAS_CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN=
